 it was a  malfunction or nerves only he knows  abdel slam escaped and was eventually  arrested in belgium after four months on  the run in court for day one he was the  most aggressive and vocal of the accused  when the judge asked his occupation he  said he had left all professions to  become a soldier of the islamic state  the judge responded with a joke saying  basically he'd heard it was an interim  position abdul salaam would go on to say  he was being treated like a dog and  ranted until his microphone was cut off  bataclan survivor thierry malee says he  was surprised by how much seeing  abdullah in person hit him but that he's  not scared and will face him in court  now the high profile of this trial has  the country on high alert and it's  likely to last a verdict isn't expected  until late may of next year mike  armstrong global news  a russian government minister who once  served in president vladimir putin's  security detail has died in the arctic  while trying to save the life of a film  director you have jenny zinechev headed  the high profile emergencies ministry  since 2018. the ministry says the  55-year-old died during a training  exercise the exact circumstances of his  death remain unclear officials say he  jumped from a cliff in an apparent  rescue attempt  ferocious storms tear through parts of  southwestern ontario coming up the trail  of damage people are now forced to clean  up plus powerful goals america's plan to  rely on solar energy and a towering  figure of racism removed  this is a look at the debris that was  strewn about at a farm in lucknow  ontario just north of goderich residents  are spending the day cleaning up  yesterday's severe storms moved through  parts of southern ontario prompting  environment canada to issue tornado  warnings for some areas  god those sparks are getting on the car  now  one toronto family woke up to this a  tree branch had fallen on a power line  the line then hit their car and sparked  a fire luckily no one was injured  i was quite worried last night to be  honest that there may be an ex an  explosion or something like that because  there was a lot of water out here  and then with the  the flame coming off the the wire  who knows what could have happened  hydro one says power has been restored  to more than 65 000 customers affected  by last night's storm crews continue to  work on other hard-hit areas  particularly along the shore of lake  huron  in mexico at least one person was killed  when a powerful earthquake struck near  acapulco last night  the magnitude 7 quake was felt hundreds  of miles away in mexico city it struck  just before 9 p.m and nearly 100  aftershocks were reported before dawn  the quake triggered widespread blackouts  landslides and several gas leaks no  major damage to buildings has been  reported  solar strategies still ahead the bright  plan for renewable energy in the u.s  one of america's largest confederate  monuments has come down the six-meter  bronze statue of general robert e lee  was removed from a pedestal in virginia  it overlooked the capitol for more than  a century but in recent years had become  a target of protesters looking to remove  symbols of racism the monument was  broken into pieces which will be put  into storage the graffiti covered  pedestal will stay for now  the biden administration has released an  ambitious renewable energy plan a new  report from the u.s department of energy  shows that by 2035 solar energy has the  potential to power 40 percent of  america's electricity and employ as many  as 1.5 million people without raising  electricity costs for consumers that  goal is contingent on congress passing  legislation that prioritizes and  supports renewable energy as well as the  widespread adoption of solar power it  currently accounts for about three  percent of the u.s electricity supply  britney spears is another step closer to  taking full control of her life in an  unexpected move her father filed to end  the court-ordered conservatorship that  has managed the singer's life and money  for 13 years the 39-year-old has tried  to remove her father from her case twice  in the last two years claiming that her  conservatorship was abusive jamie spears  took over his daughter's affairs after  she went through a mental health crisis  in 2008. he denies any allegations of  abuse and says he only wants what's best  for his daughter the decision now rests  with a judge and that is global national  for this wednesday night i'm robin gill  tonight your canada is near lord minster  saskatchewan thank you for watching and  be sure to tune in tomorrow when donna  friesen will broadcast from vedeck nova  scotia and i'll see you again this  weekend have a great night  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]
 

